00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:02.629 align:start position:0%
 
welcome to an introduction to omics  logic a little bit about me my name is  laura murray as elia mentioned i am the  educational program coordinator here at  pine biotech  i have a background in gaining my  bachelor's degree in microbiology and  i'm currently finishing up my master's  degree in biology and bioinformatics  my focus and areas of expertise are in  metagenomics transcriptomics and  genomics  and my most recent research was in  analyzing the metagenomics of deep sea  hydrothermal vents  and which bacterial communities reside  there  so in this presentation i will explain  the current challenges and limitations  in bioinformatics  i will describe how we aim to address  these challenges with the omex logic  portal  i will describe bloom's taxonomy for  learn learning progression and how it  can be used in bioinformatics coursework  we will explore the omixlogic portal and  how it utilizes bloom's taxonomy and  structuring its courses  pipelines and projects  and finally i will describe several  outcomes of the omics logic portal  so what are some of the challenges that  the field of bioinformatics is currently  facing  to begin this field is constantly  growing and developing new tech and  software to improve processing time and  power  the data sets that are analyzed are also  usually very large and take immense  amounts of computing power and memory  that many personal computers just don't  have  also despite being publicly available  data are also usually complex to access  and coding knowledge is usually required  to do so  similarly analysis pipelines and  programs require coding knowledge that  many biologists don't have  in the university setting students have  the opportunity to learn the background  information of designing and  implementing a bioinformatics project  but don't receive practical hands-on  experience with the full workflow due to  the limitations mentioned previously  similarly faculty faces challenges with  being able to cover a diverse range of  topics especially if they are  specialized in a certain area of  bioinformatics or if they are unfamiliar  with bioinformatics in general  for example a professor whose research  focuses on oncogene expression might not  know much about the meta genomics of  seawater  so in order to overcome these challenges  the omixologic portal was developed this  program aims to standardize organize and  systemize bioinformatics training in  order to make these analyses usable for  any biologist or clinician  there are some traditional problems with  the standardization of bioinformatics  coursework  materials for courses are usually  developed in-house taught sporadically  and are rarely updated  the omixlogic portal introduces new  material that keeps up with new  technology  these courses also need to be organized  because the challenge is to combine  several different topics together the  flow and transitions between subjects  needs to be developed  this is addressed at omics logic through  introductory material being woven  throughout the course  the last challenge we face is  systemization how can you know that  someone is stuck and needs help or allow  someone to run forward  to address this omixlogic uses  standardized modules and interactive  sessions beginning with mastering  terminology and concepts to implementing  these concepts with real data sets in a  project-based approach  so here's an overview of the learning  process so in order to create a clear  path of skill development omics logic  employs the bloom's taxonomy levels of  learning  this approach starts with the basics  students recall facts and terminology  and are able to repeat and memorize the  material  with this base the learning builds to  conceptual knowledge being able to  understand concepts and apply  information to new situations  the student will then be able to analyze  data by drawing connections and evaluate  when to use certain methods  this leads them to the highest level of  learning the ability to design and  create original work  so how do omixlogic resources help  advance bioinformatics teaching  omixlogic is a portal for practical and  theoretical learning of bioinformatics  composed of courses designed to take you  through the theoretical knowledge  omixlogic takes a combination of  training modules data analysis tools  curated project data sets and  interactive sessions with mentors to  give a student a clear path at the  bloom's taxonomy pyramid  no matter what the user's initial  experience with bioinformatics is  omixlogic is a useful tool for gaining a  baseline knowledge of the theory behind  bioinformatics analysis of large data  sets  an introduction to basic coding  languages like r and python or beginning  a data analysis project  so these six courses were taken from the  core omixlogic curriculum available  online  beginning with an introduction to the  applications of bioinformatics in an  overview of data types the student is  able to learn terminology and factual  knowledge to build upon from there  genomics transcriptomics metagenomics  epigenomics and data science are  introduced  each course starts with important terms  and concepts and then introduces case  studies and pipelines related to each  one  this allows the student to gain the  conceptual knowledge in order to begin  their own projects  so omixlogic also expands upon its basic  core curriculum with specialization  track projects bioinformatics methods  are best learned in the context of real  case studies prepared by our network of  mentors and collaborators that  illustrate how various bioinformat  bioinformatics methods and omics data  types are used in current research both  in medicine and in biotechnology  agriculture and even astrobiology  the projects are prepared by taking  publicly available data sets and using  them to explore and understand both the  research challenge and the analysis path  to extract meaningful insights from  complex omics data  the omixlogic portal gives students  options for analyzing a given data set  either a codependent path or a code  independent path  these datasets and associated  publications can be used in several ways  so like i mentioned you can learn  bioinformatics without coding at any  coding experience at all for that in  each project we explain the analysis  pipelines on the user-friendly t-bioinfo  platform for big data analysis  you can also learn the scripts behind  many of the steps learning to wrangle  clean and visualize and analyze data in  popular languages like r and python in  order to create your own analyses  finally you can hear about the projects  and their research applications in our  mentor guided programs where experts  share their experience and support  research projects developed by you  so here's an example of the code  independent pipeline the pipeline  builder interface on the t bioinfo  platform is a color-coded pipeline that  helps establish a logical connection  between the technical names of data  analysis methods and the logical steps  needed to build the fold pipeline  data is put in as an input file and then  analyses can be chosen based off of the  type of research  each analysis is separated into three  colors  blue for pre-processing red for mapping  and green for quantification each time  you click a button a pop-up will contain  additional information useful for  building the pipeline  the ease of the color-coded buttons  allows programs to be run without any  coding knowledge  interactive outputs allow for easy  visualization of the data  several demo pipelines with real data  sets are available for students to  practice the workflow including demos on  genomic variant calling of cancer cell  lines  16s amplicon analysis on diet and its  effects on the microbiome and a pipeline  for examining a phylogenetic analysis of  ebola virus  so after using the tbiwinfo platform to  visualize the pipelines and practice  analyzing students are then able to take  their theoretical knowledge the remember  and understand level of blooms  and apply that in a project the apply  analyze and evaluate level of blooms  then students are able to check their  comprehension with levels and badges  certificates of completion and tests  similarly faculty could be should be  able to assign the omixlogic portal to  their students with the understanding  that it will give them holistic and  comprehensive knowledge of  bioinformatics beginning with the bytes  and molecules course and on to designing  their own question based project  so omixlogic employs a hybrid approach  combining learning and research to  ensure that students are building off of  the first level of bloom's taxonomy  omics logic tracks progress with  activities like pipelines coding and  literature reviews quizzes on topics key  terms and important questions and covers  a broad range of topics like biomedical  research biotechnology and agriculture  then students are able to continue their  knowledge base with a research  assessment making sure they are able to  understand methods challenges and  results as well as being able to  comprehend primary research literature  and recreate the methodology  they should be able to ask questions  based on data exploration this leads to  the ability to encounter errors in their  analysis  apply theoretical knowledge of why those  errors are occurring and find a solution  bioinformatics uniquely combines life  science terms with data science skills  which allows researchers to answer life  science questions with reproducible data  analysis methods  so omics logic research fellows are able  to ask research questions about any  bioinformatics topic leading to a  diverse range of projects from analyzing  affected biological pathways and  multiple sclerosis to brain metastases  due to small cell lung cancer these  students are able to apply what they've  learned in the coursework work with a  group of professional mentors and submit  their projects on the portal for review  so students should then be able to reach  the highest level of bloom's taxonomy  create  this is achieved through the creation of  their own analysis project for example  cement dolonier an undergraduate  research at belchesia university in  istanbul turkey who finished her  omixlogic training was able to work on a  project involving chronic lymphocytic  leukemia a type of blood cancer that has  a very heterogeneous biological  background and diverse treatment  strategies  from her work with omics logic samea's  work was able to be published with the  columbia undergraduate science journal  here at first she elicited 870  significantly differentially expressed  protein coding genes that were involved  in the biogenesis and processing of rna  consequently these findings led our  study to investigate non-coding rna 33  long non-coding rnas were found to be  significantly differentially expressed  among two conditions based on  differential gene expression analysis  so not only does omics logic collaborate  with undergraduate students as seen with  cma but projects with graduate students  and other researchers are common as well  here is a poster presentation for a  project done in collaboration between  naguchi memorial institute for medical  research and pine biotech  here's our team at pine biotech who are  involved with the project dr mohit  mazumdar dr harpreet kaur and elia  brodsky as well as our collaborators at  the university of ghona dr anita gansa  and dr benedicta mensah  this poster was on plasmodium falcibrium  the parasite causing malaria in its  apical membrane antigen the roctry neck  two protein binding which is a critical  interaction for plasmodium falcipromyzoa  invasion of the human host red blood  cells  several proposed malaria vaccine  candidates are designed to prevent such  finding in limit merizoa entry which  have been studied with variable success  at in vitro in early clinical trial  stages  by performing haplotype network analysis  of genomic sequencing data from sites  with variable infection rates comparing  our data with malaria gen repository  from another region in ghana  and mapping genomic variants onto the  protein structures they arrived at  preliminary conclusions about local  variation and immunogenic epitope  affecting variants for consideration  in this poster preliminary findings were  shared that suggest that genomic data  can be used to develop a local strategy  for efficacious vaccine design against  pfelcipram blood stage infection in  ghana and surrounding regions  so omixlogic is proud to collaborate  with many diverse programs across the  globe  we also work with over 15 000 students  at community college like glendale  community college top tier universities  like georgetown university as well as 20  universities around the world  omixlogic is also proud to partner with  nappy the national association of idea  principal investigators  nappy seeks to elevate bioinformatics  research in areas of the us that are  traditionally underfunded for example in  puerto rico  louisiana  and west virginia  nabi puts an emphasis on inclusion  making sure that as many people have the  opportunity to get involved with  bioinformatics research as possible  omixlogic is proud to mirror that  emphasis of inclusion with adding many  free course options  giving students asynchronous resources  to complete whenever their busy schedule  allows and pairing them with  professional mentors who can offer  guidance in getting involved in the  field of bioinformatics  so in this presentation i explained a  bit about the current challenges and  limitations in bioinformatics  i described how we aim to address these  challenges with the omics logic platform  we discussed bloom's taxonomy for  learning progression and how it can be  used in bioinformatics coursework  we also explored the omixlogic program  fundamentals and how it utilizes bloom's  taxonomy and structuring its courses  pipelines and projects  and we finally described several  outcomes of the omics logic program  so if you're wanting to know how to get  started the omics logic portal is easy  and free for anyone to register with  many courses available at no cost  there are also several upcoming programs  that as a student you can get involved  in  this is a program for data science for  biomedical data there's also one for  genomic data analysis and one on an  introduction to big data bioinformatics  as a member of faculty  please reach out to us about learning  more on integrating omixlogic courses  into your own bioinformatics curriculum  so thank you all are there any questions

